# Copy to `.env` and fill in from your Supabase project's API settings.
#
# `.env` is gitignored. Nothing here is read by the app yet — the extension takes
# its cloud configuration from the side panel's Settings tab, because the corpus
# belongs to whoever is holding the browser and not to whoever built it. These
# exist for the tooling around it: seeding, the Step 4 Netlify Function, and
# having the values in one place instead of in a browser form.
#
# ## Which project this is
#
# The *owner* project — one person's corpus, holding `sources`, `chunks` and
# `deletions` (see SCHEMA_SQL in src/rag/sync.ts). Every user of Autorag keeps
# their own, which is what makes corpora private by default.
#
# It is NOT the directory project. That one is separate, holds `profiles`,
# `sessions`, `invites` and `demo_usage`, and exists so people can find each
# other. Keeping them apart is a security property: a join code hands out this
# project's publishable key, and if the directory lived here that key would also
# address the table holding other people's credentials.

# The project REST URL, e.g. https://<ref>.supabase.co
SUPABASE_URL=

# `sb_publishable_…`. Safe in client code by design: it grants nothing on its
# own, and row-level security scopes every row to the signed-in user's
# auth.uid(). The credential that actually matters is the session JWT, which is
# per-user and expires.
SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=

# `sb_secret_…`. **Bypasses row-level security entirely.** Server-side only —
# a Netlify Function or a local script, never a browser.
#
# Note that no variable in this file carries the `NEXT_PUBLIC_` prefix, and that
# is the only reason Next cannot inline this into the static export. Do not add
# the prefix to "make it work" in a component; if a component needs it, the
# design is wrong.
SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY=

# Where the project publishes the public keys its JWTs are signed with. Present
# because this project uses the newer asymmetric signing rather than the legacy
# shared secret; needed only if something has to verify a token itself.
SUPABASE_JWKS_URL=
